// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`devto markdown > matches the snapshot 1`] = `
"Prometheus is cheap right up to the point where it is not, and the line between the two is almost never the number of samples.

## Part 1: What Prometheus stores

> **Big Word Alert: time series** A time series is one metric name plus one exact set of label values, and the sequence of timestamped numbers collected for it.

![The head block and the blocks on disk](https://www.example-blog.dev/images/blogs/head-block.svg)

## Part 2: Where cardinality costs you

| Label                            | Why it explodes                     | Where it belongs instead            |
| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Pod name on an autoscaling fleet | Unique forever, replaced constantly | Logs, with the Pod name in the line |
| Request or trace ID              | Unique per request                  | Traces or logs                      |

\`\`\`promql
count by (__name__) ({__name__=~".+"})
\`\`\`

> **Note:** Aside: this is Prometheus specifically
>
> Other time series stores make different trade-offs, but series count is the cost driver everywhere.

> **Interactive diagram: x.** Open it on the original post: https://www.example-blog.dev/blog/prometheus-cardinality-explained#x

---

*Originally published at [example-blog.dev](https://www.example-blog.dev/blog/prometheus-cardinality-explained).*
"
`;
